---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy | Aniloom Technologies" description="How Aniloom Technologies handles website inquiries, AniShot diagnostic reports, email communications, and hosting.">
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="section-shell legal-page">
      <article class="article-shell">
        <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p>Effective date: October 9, 2026</p>
        <div class="article-content">
          <p>
            Aniloom Technologies LLC respects your privacy. This site is a marketing website and
            informational publication site. We keep data collection minimal.
          </p>
          <h2>Information We Collect</h2>
          <p>
            If you use our contact form, we process your email address and project description,
            together with a selected package when applicable. If you email us directly, we receive
            the information you choose to include in your message.
          </p>
          <h2>Automatic Data</h2>
          <p>
            Contact form requests are processed through Cloudflare Workers and sent to our inbox
            through Resend. Cloudflare Turnstile checks submissions for automated abuse. These
            providers process the request information needed to deliver messages and protect the form.
            The form checks email format but does not verify that you own the mailbox.
            The website is hosted on GitHub Pages and loads fonts from Google Fonts. Your browser
            connects to these providers, which may process technical request information such as
            your IP address and browser details under their own policies.
          </p>
          <p>
            Spam protection uses your connecting IP address. Our application stores keyed hashes
            and short-lived submission records for rate limits and duplicate prevention, normally
            removed within about 24 hours. These records do not contain your message or plain-text
            email address. Provider infrastructure and our inbox have their own retention practices.
          </p>
          <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
          <p>
            We use information you send us to respond to inquiries, evaluate project fit, and
            communicate about potential services.
          </p>
          <h2>Sharing</h2>
          <p>
            We do not sell personal information. We may share information with service providers
            involved in hosting, security, or communications when reasonably necessary to operate
            the site or respond to your request.
          </p>
          <h2>Data Retention</h2>
          <p>
            We retain inquiry emails and related business communications for as long as reasonably
            necessary for operations, legal compliance, or recordkeeping.
          </p>
          <h2 id="anishot">AniShot Screen Capture</h2>
          <p>
            AniShot processes screen images and annotations on your Mac. It captures only when you
            request a screenshot, holds the session image in memory, and releases it when the session
            closes. It does not capture audio or maintain continuous screen history. Copy uses the
            macOS clipboard; Save writes a file to the destination you confirm. Share gives the image
            to the macOS service you select. Clipboard syncing, synced folders and sharing services
            may transfer exported images under their own settings and policies.
          </p>
          <p>
            AniShot keeps diagnostic history locally by default, for up to seven days within about
            1 MB. Settings → Appearance → Diagnostics lets you disable or clear it. History includes
            recent app actions, capture durations, tool sizes and error codes. Diagnostic fields
            exclude screenshots, typed annotations, clipboard contents, file paths and raw error messages.
          </p>
          <p>
            Pressing Send Report in Settings → Support sends retained diagnostic events, app and Mac
            details, a random installation ID and your optional comment to our private Cloudflare service.
            Reports are sent only when you press that button. An email address or account is not required.
            The installation ID is generated locally on the first send attempt and reused in later
            reports; it does not use your hardware serial number or computer name. The report ID shown
            after successful sending can identify a deletion request. Check personal or confidential
            information you choose to write in the comment before sending.
          </p>
          <p>
            Active reports are retained for at most 30 days, within the latest 100 reports.
            Cloudflare recovery states can retain deleted data for up to another 30 days.
            Reports require authenticated access and have no public download URL. Cloudflare processes
            connecting IP addresses to deliver and protect requests; our service stores keyed IP hashes
            for ten-minute rate limits rather than raw addresses. Provider infrastructure has its own
            operational processing. Clearing local history does not delete reports already sent.
          </p>
          <p>
            The website download checks aniloom.tech for signed updates through Sparkle. Automatic
            checks can be disabled in Settings → Updates. Hosting receives ordinary request metadata,
            including the IP address and app/Sparkle versions. Screenshots and diagnostic history are
            excluded from update requests, and Sparkle system profiling is disabled. A Store-specific
            package uses App Store updates and excludes Sparkle. AniShot has no advertising or tracking
            integration. Email correspondence, if you choose to contact us separately, follows the
            support and retention practices above.
          </p>
          <h2>Your Choices</h2>
          <p>
            You may contact us at <a href="mailto:support@aniloom.tech">support@aniloom.tech</a> to
            request correction or deletion of information you have sent us, subject to legal or
            operational obligations.
          </p>
          <h2>Changes</h2>
          <p>
            We may update this policy from time to time. Material changes will be reflected on this
            page with an updated effective date.
          </p>
        </div>
      </article>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
